ARM: dts: unisoc: rda8810pl-orangepi-i96: pin CMA inside the IFC DMA window

The IFC DMA engine addresses only the first 64 MB of DRAM (26-bit
start_addr, offset from 0x80000000). Pin the default CMA pool inside
that window so dma_alloc_coherent() users — in particular the rda-mmc
bounce buffer — always land at a DMA-reachable address on this 256 MB
board.

Local backport addition to the "RDA8810PL SD/MMC support" series.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-local workaround pending proper dma-ranges support]

Signed-off-by: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
---

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/rda8810pl-orangepi-i96.dts
@@ -28,6 +28,25 @@
 		reg = <0x80000000 0x10000000>;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <1>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/*
+		 * The IFC DMA reaches only 0x80000000..0x83ffffff (26-bit
+		 * start_addr). Keep the default CMA pool inside that window
+		 * so coherent allocations (rda-mmc bounce) are reachable.
+		 */
+		linux,cma {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			reusable;
+			size = <0x2000000>;
+			alloc-ranges = <0x80000000 0x4000000>;
+			linux,cma-default;
+		};
+	};
+
 	vdd_sdmmc: regulator-fixed {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vdd_sdmmc";
